% ===================================================================== %
%  References for:
%    p2p-inference.tex  Quantifying Carbon, Water, Cost, and Capability in
%                       Peer-to-Peer Inference
%    adaptation.tex     Teaching at the Edge
%
%  Every entry has a locator or DOI and has undergone metadata and locator
%  triage. Exact claim support is recorded in paper/CITATION_CLAIM_REVIEW.md;
%  that semantic check still requires reading each source against each nearby
%  sentence. Author lists are copied from the identified source where verified.
%  Every entry describing third-party work carries a resolvable URL or DOI. So
%  does every entry describing this study's own artifacts, except
%  autoyou_support2026: that material is genuinely not redistributable, and a
%  citation should not promise a locator that does not resolve.
%
%  Four entries in an earlier version of this file were wrong in ways a
%  reader could not have detected, and are recorded here so the correction
%  is auditable rather than silent:
%
%    * schneider2025 (was `faiz2025`) carried the correct arXiv ID and
%      title but an invented author list. The paper is by Schneider et
%      al. (Google), not Faiz et al.
%    * devriesgao2025 (was `devriesgao2026`) had the wrong title, the
%      wrong article ID, and split the single author Alex de Vries-Gao
%      into two people by inventing a co-author.
%    * ni2025benchmarks (was `mmlu_survey2025`) had the author field
%      literally set to {Anonymous}, and was cited by no manuscript while
%      supplying the benchmark figures behind the hard-reasoning ratio.
%    * uptime2025 stated a title that does not appear at the URL given.
%
%    * nvidia_rtx4090 (was `promptquorum2026`) cited a third-party blog
%      whose own title stated 575 W for the RTX 4090 -- that is the RTX
%      5090's board power. Replaced with the vendor specification (450 W).
%    * qwen38_2026 was attributed to the Qwen team but pointed at a
%      third-party SEO article; repointed at the official model card. The
%      separate qwen38_ollama2026 entry now carries the distribution-size
%      claim so the two kinds of evidence are not conflated.
%    * autoyou2026edge named a manuscript that does not exist.
%
%  Three of the four entries describing this study's own artifacts point at
%  the public repository that holds them. The fourth, autoyou_support2026,
%  carries no URL because that material is genuinely not redistributable, and
%  every finding depending on it is marked not independently validated.
%
%  Two further entries had placeholder author fields of the form
%  {LoRP-TTS authors}. Both concerned text-to-speech adaptation, neither
%  was cited by either manuscript, and both have been removed rather than
%  repaired: they concern a line of work outside the scope of these papers.
% ===================================================================== %


